doc:sec-20a-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20A(1) Objections to re-submitted draft Plan" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Territory planning authority continues to object to any aspect of the draft Plan re-submitted to the Minister, the Authority must attach to the draft Plan a statement of its reasons for not accommodating the objection." ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988-sec-20a-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20A(2) Objections to re-submitted draft Plan"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20a-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the Minister receives a statement from the Authority under subsection (1), the Minister, after consultation with the Executive, must give a written direction to the Authority:  (a) to disregard the objection; or  (b) to alter the draft Plan to accommodate the objection wholly or partly.   The National Capital Plan  Part III Preparation of National Capital Plan  Division 2  Section 21  Australian Capital Territory (Planning and Land Management) Act 1988 Compilation date: 1/7/18 Registered: 6/8/18" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If the Minister receives a statement from the Authority under subsection (1), the Minister, after consultation with the Executive, must give a written direction to the Authority:  (a) to disregard the objection; or  (b) to alter the draft Plan to accommodate the objection wholly or partly.   The National Capital Plan  Part III Preparation of National Capital Plan  Division 2  Section 21  Australian Capital Territory (Planning and Land Management) Act 1988 Compilation date: 1/7/18 Registered: 6/8/18"@en ;
