    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The Plan may be prepared in separate stages or parts and, in such a case, sections 14 to 23 (both inclusive) apply as if references in those sections to the Plan were references to such a stage or part of the Plan.   The Territory Plan  Part IV  Section 25  Australian Capital Territory (Planning and Land Management) Act 1988 Compilation date: 1/7/18 Registered: 6/8/18" ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988-sec-25 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "25 Territory Plan"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-25 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Assembly shall, as soon as practicable, make laws providing for:  (a) establishing a Territory planning authority; and  (b) conferring functions on the authority, including the functions of:  (i) preparing and administering a plan in respect of land, not inconsistent with the National Capital Plan; and  (ii) keeping the plan under constant review and proposing amendments to it when necessary.  (2) The object of the plan is to ensure, in a manner not inconsistent with the National Capital Plan, the planning and development of the Territory to provide the people of the Territory with an attractive, safe and efficient environment in which to live and work and have their recreation.  (3) The plan:  (a) shall define the planning principles and policies for giving effect to the object of the plan; and  (b) may include the detailed conditions of planning, design and development of land and the priorities in carrying out such planning, design and development.  (4) The laws shall include provision for:  (a) the procedure for making the plan and amendments of the plan, including a procedure for ascertaining and considering the views of the public;  (b) public notification of any directions given to the Territory planning authority by the Executive;" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Assembly shall, as soon as practicable, make laws providing for:  (a) establishing a Territory planning authority; and  (b) conferring functions on the authority, including the functions of:  (i) preparing and administering a plan in respect of land, not inconsistent with the National Capital Plan; and  (ii) keeping the plan under constant review and proposing amendments to it when necessary.  (2) The object of the plan is to ensure, in a manner not inconsistent with the National Capital Plan, the planning and development of the Territory to provide the people of the Territory with an attractive, safe and efficient environment in which to live and work and have their recreation.  (3) The plan:  (a) shall define the planning principles and policies for giving effect to the object of the plan; and  (b) may include the detailed conditions of planning, design and development of land and the priorities in carrying out such planning, design and development.  (4) The laws shall include provision for:  (a) the procedure for making the plan and amendments of the plan, including a procedure for ascertaining and considering the views of the public;  (b) public notification of any directions given to the Territory planning authority by the Executive;"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d63b52eff72c6dd10329ddd61e18b31a6420f6883f49e8c794debbe6e302ee5d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988-sec-25-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988-sec-25-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988-sec-25-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988-sec-25-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988.pdf, p.21" .
doc:sec-25 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "25 Territory Plan" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Assembly shall, as soon as practicable, make laws providing for:  (a) establishing a Territory planning authority; and  (b) conferring functions on the authority, including the functions of:  (i) preparing and administering a plan in respect of land, not inconsistent with the National Capital Plan; and  (ii) keeping the plan under constant review and proposing amendments to it when necessary.  (2) The object of the plan is to ensure, in a manner not inconsistent with the National Capital Plan, the planning and development of the Territory to provide the people of the Territory with an attractive, safe and efficient environment in which to live and work and have their recreation.  (3) The plan:  (a) shall define the planning principles and policies for giving effect to the object of the plan; and  (b) may include the detailed conditions of planning, design and development of land and the priorities in carrying out such planning, design and development.  (4) The laws shall include provision for:  (a) the procedure for making the plan and amendments of the plan, including a procedure for ascertaining and considering the views of the public;  (b) public notification of any directions given to the Territory planning authority by the Executive;" ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer .

