    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-37-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The Minister may appoint a person to act as a non-executive member referred to in subsection 33(3) or (4) during any period, or during all periods:  (a) when there is a vacancy in the office of a non-executive member, whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office; or  (b) when a non-executive member is acting as Chairperson, is absent from Australia or is, for any other reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The Minister may appoint a person to act as a non-executive member referred to in subsection 33(3) or (4) during any period, or during all periods:  (a) when there is a vacancy in the office of a non-executive member, whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office; or  (b) when a non-executive member is acting as Chairperson, is absent from Australia or is, for any other reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
