doc:sec-65 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "65 Variation or revocation of NCDC policies during transition" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "period  (1) During the transition period, an NCDC policy still in effect may be:  (a) revoked wholly or partly by the National Capital Plan; or  (b) varied under Division 4 or 5." ;
    cof:pageNumber "41"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988-sec-66 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "66 NCDC policies after transition period"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-66 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) at the end of the transition period, an NCDC policy, or part of such a policy, is still in effect;  (b) the policy, or that part of the policy, is such that it could be part of the National Capital Plan; and  (c) either House of the Parliament, within 6 sitting days of that House after the end of the transition period, passes a resolution that the policy, or that part of the policy, is to become part of the National Capital Plan; the policy, or that part of the policy, becomes part of the National Capital Plan, and may be varied or revoked accordingly.  (2) On the day after the last day on which a resolution could be passed as described in paragraph (1)(c), an NCDC policy, or part of such a policy, that is still in effect and has not become part of the National Capital Plan under subsection (1) shall be taken to be part of the Territory Plan, and may be varied or revoked accordingly.   Transitional provisions  Part X Variation of NCDC policies by Authority  Division 4  Section 67  Australian Capital Territory (Planning and Land Management) Act 1988 Compilation date: 1/7/18 Registered: 6/8/18" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) at the end of the transition period, an NCDC policy, or part of such a policy, is still in effect;  (b) the policy, or that part of the policy, is such that it could be part of the National Capital Plan; and  (c) either House of the Parliament, within 6 sitting days of that House after the end of the transition period, passes a resolution that the policy, or that part of the policy, is to become part of the National Capital Plan; the policy, or that part of the policy, becomes part of the National Capital Plan, and may be varied or revoked accordingly.  (2) On the day after the last day on which a resolution could be passed as described in paragraph (1)(c), an NCDC policy, or part of such a policy, that is still in effect and has not become part of the National Capital Plan under subsection (1) shall be taken to be part of the Territory Plan, and may be varied or revoked accordingly.   Transitional provisions  Part X Variation of NCDC policies by Authority  Division 4  Section 67  Australian Capital Territory (Planning and Land Management) Act 1988 Compilation date: 1/7/18 Registered: 6/8/18"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "417874b3cb44597b8f5f548c9b2daeea23e7d9bd7ad0c9a3236815b920495806" ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988-sec-66-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-act-1988-sec-66-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
